[{:seon.task/name "a-commit-reaches-only-the-readers-of-what-it-moved"
  :seon.task/plan "STATUS (root's independent review, 2026-11-15 17:25, notes reactive-core-review-2026-11-15-1725.md; sound with changes): NOT YET BUILT, whatever the text below says: the typed :seon.ratom/no-owner refusal and its proof a-reaction-made-outside-an-owner-is-refused, the height-ordered flush and its proofs (diamond, deeper source, deep chain), the typed cycle error. Their work is seon.ratom/the-core-is-correct-before-a-reader-moves, the next core slice. Land A (0056478b93) built only the throwing reader as its own error, :auto-run :queue and the bounded flush! n. DELIBERATE DEVIATIONS FROM REAGENT (each with its reason; the reviewer root starts checks them): (1) a reader whose run throws is its own error, raised when it is read, and flush! and commit! never throw: Reagent rethrows an auto-run reaction's throw from flush!, but here flush! runs inside an owner proc's step, so one malformed stored value read by one reader (a recorded error's row) would end the step and leave every later reader of that commit untold; the throw belongs to the reader that met it (2e5533afb4; seon.ratom-test's four exception tests state the rule). (2) A Store's commit! wakes only the readers its index names for the commit's datoms, where Reagent notifies every watch of a changed atom: a store's value is a db, and a reader depends on the datoms it read, not on the whole value. (3) A reaction runs only in its owner's step; one dirtied under another owner reaches it as a message (Flow's five rules). LAND A PROGRESS: health's recorded report as reactions, seon.problems/recorded-live, recorded-sync!, recorded-report (per-error row reactions; the set diffed only when it moved; each class a sorted map, a change O(log n)); proof seon.problems-test/a-move-that-touches-no-error-reruns-no-error-row green (equal to report; an untouched move reruns no row; a new error adds one row and reruns none). Left: the render proc's Store fed by advance-main, health! reading the live report, its own d/datoms-diff deleted, and before/after on the standing root. WEB'S REVIEW OF LAND A (16:2x): YES, with 4 conditions, each in the build: (1) BUG 2 first [read ratom.clj:529]: an auto-run reaction runs with check false (-run this false), outside Reagent's catch, and commit! runs it inline, so one malformed stored error throws out of the render proc's step and the readers after it are never told; every run goes through the catching path (the named edge failure-points.md declares for a reaction's run), its throw the reaction's state, and the commit goes on. (2) The report is the delta fold, not a reaction that derefs all 4,066 rows: after flush!, the owner step replaces the rows that reran in the report it holds (report' = report with the changed rows replaced), so a new error costs its row, never 4,066 derefs. (3) The api's repeat counts (seon.problems/with-fold) are no db fact: the fold step takes them as its input by plain deref, never through a ratom view (BUG 1). (4) Proofs: health-moved-is-health on the standing store's real db; a move that adds one error reruns exactly one row, ticks within 2x of the row (~39k) plus the fold step. The tile on root's debug page derefs the report and redraws only when the report value changes. WEB'S CORE EDGE CASES (2026-11-15 16:1x, real data, repros /tmp/web3-rt*.clj): GREEN: a retraction reruns its reader (answers nil) [dc412954]; nesting under an owner, the child then the parent [c0fbdbb0]; a turn-shaped pull reruns only that call's reaction, commit 20.7k, pull 9.6k ticks [c66badee]. BUG 2, fixed IN LAND A (health's rows run in the render proc's step): a reaction whose run throws makes commit! throw to its caller [dc412954], so the watchers after it in that commit are never told and the thrower answers its old value; a run's throw is that reaction's value as data (its error, Reagent's caught state) and the commit goes on to every other reader. HAZARD, fixed IN LAND A: a reaction made with no owner bound has its dirtying dropped (a deref answers stale, no error): making one outside an owner is refused, a typed :seon.ratom/no-owner. Proofs, red first: seon.ratom-test/a-reader-that-throws-is-its-own-error-and-the-commit-reaches-the-rest; seon.ratom-test/a-reaction-made-outside-an-owner-is-refused. FOUND BY WEB (2026-11-15 16:0x) [M web result/d16e7b01, repro /tmp/web3-rt5.clj]: a reaction reading through ratom/ref-view never reruns on a swap! of its ref (dirty? false, its value stale), while one reading @ref does. Cause [read ratom.clj:517-525]: -update-watching drops every captured view read on purpose (a read through a view is no source: the walk keeps it as a value and matches it itself, reads-of and reached). So no reaction over a view can be woken, which blocks switch-over item 2 (web's pages as reactions), not Land A (health reads the db through the Store). Fix, runtime's, before web's land: a captured [src path kind] watches src's ref, and a change dirties the reaction only when (changes old new) reaches one of its reads (seon.ratom/reached, written), per ref an index of path reads as the Store indexes datom keys. Proof, red first: seon.ratom-test/a-reaction-over-a-view-reruns-when-its-path-moves (web's repro: the swap! reruns it, a swap! of another path does not). LAND A (runtime, 2026-11-15 15:5x; root's ruling: the core live with health's classes as its first callers, on web's design seon.problems/laws-and-health-are-one-set-of-live-classes point 2; web reviews health, flow the commit feed). PRIOR WORK: this task's Store holding the one index (seon.db/reads-add/readers in seon.ratom, branch 1f308afab2: commit! wakes only the named readers); seon.ratom/track and make-reaction (ratom.clj:577-655); the render proc's health! (render/proc.clj:809-825), which calls seon.problems/health-moved on each move of main with advance-main's moved datoms. MEASURED [attached agent, main's real 11-datom move]: health-moved 180M ticks / 906 MB a move [result/b7b84570], of which report-with 176M / 885 MB [result/aa0b4db9]; within it, 4,066 recorded errors' rows at ~39k ticks each = 160M, and 27 open tasks' rows at ~182k each = 4.9M [result/d68abfc9]. So a move of 11 datoms costs 4,066 error rows that nothing moved. DESIGN: one Store mechanism, one instance per owner proc (root 15:5x asked; flow decides): a reaction runs only in its owner's step (seon.ratom-test/a-reaction-runs-only-in-its-owners-step), so a Store shared across procs would make every other owner's reaction cross-owner, a message per dirty reader; each owner's Store indexes only its own readers (no entry held twice) and is fed by the writer's :main notice it already takes, committed and flushed in its own step (derived-values.md section 4 step 2). Land A's owner is the render proc: its Store of main fed each move by advance-main's moved datoms (commit!, then flush!). The reconciler's and ctx's Stores come with their lands (switch-over items 4, 5). ERRORS [M result/bbe7a3d3]: all 4,066 recorded error rows are open, none ever answered (platform 2,626, agent 1,243, eval 192, effect 5): health shows them all and nothing closes one; Land A makes them cheap, not useful; closing a recorded error is filed with its owner. Health's recorded report becomes reactions over it: one reaction per error entity (its row: error-row), one per judged task (task-rows), one over the entity sets (the error signatures and the judged tasks, whole-attribute reads, rerun when one is added or gone), and the report a reaction over those rows; answers is a reaction its rows deref. The derived classes stay as health-moved carries them now (their split rows already cost 1.1M); the next land moves them. Deletes: report-with's whole read on each move (its 4,066 rows), and health's own d/datoms-diff (render/proc.clj:817), which takes advance-main's moved instead. COST: a move reruns the rows whose entities its datoms touched: an untouched move costs the index lookup, d datoms x 5 keys (~1k ticks at d = 12), against 176M; a new error, its row (~39k) plus the set's rerun; memory ~4,066 reactions x ~1.5 KB (a reaction 176 B, its keys ~135 B each) = ~6 MB. Lower bound: the d x 5 lookups. PROOFS, red first: seon.problems-test/a-move-that-touches-no-error-reruns-no-error-row (on main's real db: a move of one task datom reruns that task's rows only; ticks within 2x of the lookup bound, red today at 176M); seon.problems-test/health-moved-is-health kept (the reactive report equals a whole health read of head on real dbs); the core's own proofs on the proc's Store (seon.ratom-test/a-commit-costs-its-datoms-not-the-readers, within 2x at 10/100/1,000 readers). DECISIONS 2026-11-15 (owner via root; reviewed by flow and deps; notes runtime-core-index-plan-2026-11-15.md and runtime-reactive-plan-2026-11-15.md). Owner: index and proofs first, fully proven, the least code for 90% of the value; the core lands WITH its first real callers, proved on them: the page walk's :readers (render/queue-what-moved!) moves onto the index in the same landing, measured on the standing root after web's stall fix (the walk's readers count and per-commit cost before and after, against the ~163M post-fix cold walk, never the 6.8B debug-tab draw); health's delta fold follows as the next landing on the same core. Two reader kinds: a delta fold (state + a commit's datoms -> state') for aggregates (health, laws, the reconciler index), and a reaction for point reads (a page's component). Feed: d/changes per owner (deps proved it complete: 0 of 40 differences were net changes [deps M result/d1d98078]; 5.8M against 26.2M ticks over 406 commits [result/aa42fbe8]); the writer's notice stays {:t :commit :program-t}, each owner reads its own change in its own step, :main is a sliding buffer (flow). MEASURED today's commit! [M root result/bcecbc16]: 53.6k / 538k / 4.41M ticks at 10 / 100 / 1,000 readers for a d=10 commit none read (~5.4k a reader); a hit reruns exactly its reader. Design (~25 lines in seon.ratom, nothing new in seon.db): the Store keeps {key #{reaction}} (seon.db/reads-add, reads-drop, readers) beside its watches and holds its owner; a reaction's run updates its keys in each Store it watches, dropping them on unwatch or dispose; a run whose *owner* is not the Store's sends {:seon.ratom/keys r ks} to the Store owner's port, never a direct set! (flow's hole: the same race is latent today in watches); commit! iterates the index value captured before its loop and wakes only (readers idx datoms); a watch that is not a reaction is still called; deleted: the per-reaction reads-touched? scan on a store change. Proofs, each red first: (a) a d=10 commit at 10, 100 and 1,000 readers within 2x (82x today); (b) a 10x larger store within 2x; (c) a hot [:a a] attribute read whole by 100 readers reruns exactly 100, the commit's own cost within its budget; (d) the rerun set equals today's reads-touched? scan, generatively, seeded with deps' cases (byte-array values, [:av] through a lookup ref or ident vs the eid, cardinality-one upserts and re-assertions, a schema datom (:all) and an attribute rename, fixnum key collisions), plus the stress run at root's REPL: main's last 100 real commits replayed into 1,000 real readers, one process, no load; (e) a cross-owner key update arrives as a message. An agent, not runtime, merges and tests it. The design below stays as the height-queue and owner-step background. THE PLAN item 11 (owner-approved order, 2026-11-15): the reactive core goes live, the render proc first. The index is seon.db/reads-add, reads-drop and readers (db.clj:1236-1260, written and tested, no src caller): each reaction's key set is added under it at its run's end and dropped at its next, replacing each reaction's own watch scan, so commit! is O(d): readers over the commit's datoms. The datoms come from the writer's commit notice (:ops), never a diff (agreed with deps). Render proc first: each view becomes a reaction over its store, fed by the render proc's :main notices. Deletes in that landing: the render proc's :read-index, reindex and touched (render/proc.clj:895-914), the walk's :readers and :db-keys (render.clj:351, 1258-1261), health's second diff (proc.clj:800). Proof kept: seon.render-test/a-move-of-main-is-diffed-once-for-every-walk. Estimate: per commit, d datoms x 5 keys x one map lookup (about 1k ticks at d = 12 [M, trial A1's prototype]) plus the readers' reruns; per reaction run, its keys' add and drop, O(keys). Health, the reconciler and test verdicts follow, each its own landing that deletes what it replaces (audit target/root/audits-2026-11-15/derived-values.md section 4). The plan below stays as the height-queue and owner-step design. Owner: runtime (owner 2026-11-14 21:20: runtime owns the reactive core). Analysis approved by root and flow (notes runtime-core-map/plan-advance-heights-owner-step.md). What exists [M]: seon.ratom/commit! notifies EVERY watch of the store and each reaction tests reads-touched? over the datoms: O(readers x d), 1.25M ticks for a commit no reader read at 1,489 readers (trial A1); seon.ratom/flush! runs its queue in arrival order and an auto-run reaction runs at once inside -handle-change, so a diamond's top runs once per path (3x, ctx-r1, A1). Design: advance! (store, new-db) diffs the held head and the new head once (datahike.db/datoms-diff of plain heads, never d/history or a view), looks each moved datom's 5 keys up in {key #{reader}} kept by each reader's run (keys gained added, lost dropped, never rebuilt whole; a schema datom touches every reader) and answers {reader [datoms]}; the flush is buckets by height (1 + max height of its reactive sources, kept on the reaction), always the lowest dirty reaction next, auto-run held to the flush; a source gained mid-flush with height >= the run's raises it and its ancestors (Jane Street Incremental's adjust-heights: state.ml add_parent, adjust_heights_heap.ml), moving queued nodes, and re-queues the run unnotified when that source is still queued; effects only from a settled run; a cycle is that run's typed :seon.ratom/cycle and the flush completes. Estimate: diff O(d log32 N) ~9k ticks and ~26 KB a datom at small d; lookup O(5d) ~1k ticks, constant in readers and N; index upkeep ~160 ticks a key gained or lost; flush O(r + h + sum a) (r re-runs, h depth, a ancestors raised); d = 10: ~0.6 ms. Deletes: commit!'s match over every watch, flush!'s arrival order, auto-run's run inside -handle-change. Proofs, red first where today fails: seon.ratom-test/a-commit-costs-its-datoms-not-the-readers (T = 1, 100, 10,000; d = 1, 10; :constant in T, <= 2 x 10k ticks a datom; a forced hash collision reruns the other reader, never skips the right one); seon.ratom-test/a-commit-costs-its-datoms-not-the-store (N 10^3 vs 10^5 within 2x); seon.ratom-test/a-diamonds-top-runs-once-a-commit; seon.ratom-test/a-reaction-that-gains-a-deeper-source-runs-once-with-its-final-value; seon.ratom-test/a-deep-chain-raises-its-heights-in-its-length (h = 100, <= 60k ticks); seon.ratom-test/a-cycle-made-by-a-run-is-that-runs-typed-error. See docs/reactive.md. The diff's cost (deps, Datahike B2, 2026-11-15 06:45 [M, root's main in memory]): datahike.db/datoms-diff of plain heads costs 87, 9 and 19 KB a datom for 1, 10 and 100 scattered datoms, 1.1 KB a datom for 100 clustered, and ~60 KB a datom at a merge's d = 7,163 (the whole index decoded on both sides). The alternative, a Datahike read of the commits' datoms in (from, to], was closed with runtime-2 (06:50): advance! keeps the diff of plain heads and no range read is added to Datahike. DEPS REVIEW (Datahike side, 2026-11-15, owner's ask): APPROVED with one condition. (1) The delta feed is the commit's own changes: in-process the writer's notice :ops, across processes Datahike d/changes [M result/dbef94e1, main's last 20 commits: 185k ticks, 0.9 MB, 174 datoms, against datoms-diff of the same values at 1.03M ticks, 3.8 MB]; a held head older than the log answers :datahike/changes-unrecorded and takes one diff, then follows. (2) No branch in a key: entity ids are store-wide, so one reads index per branch store. (3) as-of and since values are a cache by db reference, never a reaction; d/history is refused for reactions. CONDITION before O(d) is claimed: the index counted by key kind on real views, since readers under [:a a] (an attribute scan records it) or :any rerun on every write to a or every commit; if they dominate, record finer keys in datahike.reads (deps' fork) rather than accept the reruns."
  :seon.task/kind :work
