 {:seon.task/name "tests-reads-on-the-core"
  :seon.task/plan "TESTS' ENGINE AND HARD CASE (tests-4, 2026-11-15): test selection is a delta fold over what a commit moved: seon.program/reach-indexed (re-answers the tests whose :reads or :takes hold a moved input key, program.clj:2364) and seon.agent/test-plan (one derivation a plan), then the results branch's verdicts at each candidate's digest (seon.proofs/verdicts-at). A test is a reader whose read keys are datom keys since landing 12 ([:e form], [:av :schema/key k], [:av :config/key k], [:av :file/path p]: seon.proofs/read-keys), so 'which tests does a commit reach' is the core's (readers idx datoms) with tests as readers. Hard cases: (1) FAN-OUT: one schema entry moves 1,570 of 2,167 tests through seon.db/entity-index's whole-class read, one config key 1,670 [M root result/d9d2d387]; the index must answer a key read by ~1,500 readers without walking each (task seon.proofs/a-new-config-key-reruns-only-the-tests-that-read-it); (2) SIZE: 259k (test, key) pairs, 4,871 distinct keys, ~118 a test [deps M target/results]; (3) COLD START: the reach graph is built per process, 293-357M ticks and 1.4-1.8 GB [M result/b28d2a1d, result/a4c6e79a], so the index must be derived once and kept, not per plan; (4) HISTORY: a verdict is keyed at a past point (its basis), and reuse asks whether its reads still hold now (seon.proofs/reused-by-reads, reads-digest), a read of two points, not only of the newest commit. MEASURED today per change of main, at the pilot agent: test-plan 44.6M ticks cold, 31.4M warm, ~143 MB [result/a57de360] (221M / 848 MB before landing 12); its reach-indexed part 21.8M; the verdict seeks over 2,185 candidates 6.3M [result/dd4228f1]. The number the move has to beat: 31.4M ticks and ~143 MB a plan; the ideal is O(moved keys x their readers) with the read-key index held, a few M ticks for a 10-datom change. THE MOVE (root, 2026-11-15): the cleanup land of task seon.proofs/a-verdict-is-an-entity-that-names-its-environment is this reader's move, the owner's switch-over item 6: verdicts as proof facts carrying :seon.reads/key-set, deleting the verdict files, .recent, reads.edn and the reuse audit, in the same land. This entry is edited only by tests; the core's entry is runtime's."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.proofs-test/a-plan-reaches-only-the-tests-that-read-what-moved}
  :seon.task/estimate #:seon.agent{test-plan {:n 2185, :order :linear, :ticks 5000000, :bytes 50000000}}
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.ratom/a-commit-reaches-only-the-readers-of-what-it-moved"}}
 {:seon.task/name "deps-reads-on-the-core"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner: deps (root, 2026-11-15: one entry per area for the reactive core, edited only by its owner; the core entry, seon.ratom/a-commit-reaches-only-the-readers-of-what-it-moved, is runtime's). DEPS (Datahike's read keys and feed), 2026-11-15, measured at root on main: (1) TODAY'S COST a change of main, d=10 datoms [M result/c0307a05]: d/changes 11.7k ticks, datahike.reads/datom-keys 2.6k (50 keys, 33 distinct: five a datom, [:e e] [:ea e a] [:a a] [:av a v] and :any), seon.db/readers 11.4k: ~26k ticks a commit before any reader runs; the bound is O(d). :any in a datom's keys is the key open-range readers are filed under, never 'touch all' (that is :all, a schema datom): a reader that records :any wakes on EVERY commit, so the core should count such readers (a row naming them), and an aggregate's reader should read an [:a a] range, never an open one. (2) WHAT EACH READ RECORDS [M result/a7d2ce00, bf2ab9bd]: a query's attribute scan and an :avet range record [:a a] (a hot attribute's every datom wakes them: the fan-out case, proof (c)); a d/history or as-of d/datoms read records [:e e]. (3) HARD CASE, A BUG: a d/pull on a temporal value (d/as-of or d/history) under d/with-reads THROWS (ClassCastException in datahike.datom/val-at-datom), while the same pull unrecorded and a recorded d/datoms on the value both work: no reaction can read history by pull until it is fixed (deps: datahike.pull-api/a-recorded-pull-on-a-temporal-value-answers). (4) A FOLD over the feed counts by net presence: d/changes nets a fact retracted and asserted again in the window to nothing (docs/storage.md#merges-read-what-changed), so a fold must read 'is the fact there at the end', never count assertions. (5) COLD START: a reaction's keys are its run's reads, so a boot reruns every reader once; a reader kept with its keys (seon.db/results-moved's :seon.proof/read-keys) skips that run. See docs/storage.md#what-a-read-scanned."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{datahike.reads-test/a-recorded-pull-on-a-history-value-records-its-entity}
  :seon.task/estimate #:datahike.reads{datom-keys {:n 10, :order :linear, :ticks 3000, :bytes 4000}}
  :seon.task/needs #{"datahike.pull-api/a-recorded-pull-on-a-temporal-value-answers" "seon.ratom/a-commit-reaches-only-the-readers-of-what-it-moved"}}
 {:seon.task/name "the-core-is-correct-before-a-reader-moves"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner: runtime; reviewer: flow. Root's order 2026-11-15 17:3x: the next core slice, after the update owner and before D; no other area moves a reader onto seon.ratom until it lands. From root's independent review (notes reactive-core-review-2026-11-15-1725.md, verdict sound with changes; prior art reagent 7ad8cdf, re-frame 1a1bf1d in reference-code). PRIOR WORK: seon.ratom (Land A, 0056478b93) and the design in a-commit-reaches-only-the-readers-of-what-it-moved. Five fixes, each with a proof seen red first: (1) No dirty reaction is stranded: flush! drains its queue before running (ratom.clj:415, 426), so a throw mid-flush strands the rest; auto-run fns and watch callbacks run outside the catch (530, 545, 558, run-in-reaction 622); no owner returns nil (394), and an owner with no port drops the reaction silently (397, 143). The render proc's owner has no port (proc.clj:799). Fix: catch at a named edge, one reaction at a time, and requeue the unrun rest; no owner or no port is a typed :seon.ratom/no-owner. (2) No glitches: commit! runs reactions inline mid-loop (527-530), so siblings see half an update. Fix: commit! only marks dirty and queues (:queue is the one mode inside an owner), and the flush runs by height. (3) Bounded, with no cycles: flush! with no n empties the queue whole, and every non-reactive deref (569) and :peek (516) calls it, bypassing :seon.config.render/flush-max. Fix: a non-reactive deref pulls only its own sources, every flush is bounded, and a cycle is a typed :seon.ratom/cycle. (4) Land A's rows read only their own entry: each of 4,066 error rows reads the whole answers map (problems.clj:1344), so one change reruns them all (~250M ticks [H]); health-more bumps :health-rev while reactions are still queued (proc.clj:950-953), mixing two points of main in one report. Fix: a row reads its own entry (track with args, or re-frame's extractor); publish only when settled. (5) One index: the render proc's :read-index (proc.clj:899-925) and the walk's :readers (render.clj:351, 667, 1258-1261) copy reads-add/readers; reactions over views never wake (ratom.clj:534), which blocks web (proof a-reaction-over-a-view-reruns-when-its-path-moves); docs/reactive.md:35 is stale. (5) shares its work with Land B. Smaller, filed with this slice: cross-owner key registration misses commits between the read and the message (142); a/put! is unbounded past 1,024 pending (142, 396); :queue reactions never auto-dispose (494); :all walks every index entry (db.clj:1290); the track cache keyed by [f args] (650) never hits for anonymous fns. COST: a commit of d datoms touching r readers, O(d + r log h) with h the height; a flush step at most flush-max (250) runs; a row's rerun O(1) per changed entry, not O(rows). MEASURED: Land A's move at 13.7M ticks [M result/a4345f35]; the coarse rows' 250M is an estimate to measure first. FLOW'S RULING on (1) and (3) as hangs (2026-11-15 evening, notes flow-ruling-reactive-core-hangs-2026-11-15.md): (1) flush! dequeues ONE reaction at a time, the queue written with the rest before each run, so every exit (a throw, or a :step-ticks budget end, which Jolt throws out of whatever runs) leaves the rest queued; each run is a named edge whose throw is that reaction's own error state (auto-run fns and watch callbacks too), and the loop goes on. Every owner has a port (the render proc's: its events chan, read by take-dirty!); a reaction under an owner with no port is a typed :seon.ratom/no-port. (3) A non-reactive deref runs only its own dirty chain (Reagent's: run f when dirty), never the queue; flush! always takes its bound (:seon.config.render/flush-max); a reaction rerun twice for one commit's generation gets :seon.ratom/cycle as its state and stops, never retried; health-more publishes :health-rev only when nothing is left, and a cycle's typed end is what ends its reposting."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.ratom-test/a-cycle-made-by-a-run-is-that-runs-typed-error seon.ratom-test/a-cross-owner-dirty-reaches-a-portless-owner-or-is-refused seon.ratom-test/a-throw-mid-flush-leaves-the-rest-queued seon.ratom-test/a-deref-runs-only-its-own-chain seon.ratom-test/a-reaction-made-outside-an-owner-is-refused seon.ratom-test/a-cycle-is-a-typed-error-not-a-livelock seon.ratom-test/a-diamonds-top-runs-once-a-commit}}]
